 35CL c  1993Ma50: a 52-MeV polarized deuteron beam at 15 nA was produced from  
 35CL2c  the Karlsruhe isochronous cyclotron at the Max-Plank-Institut fur      
 35CL3c  Kernphysik. The target was 350-mbar 99.86% enriched {+36}Ar gas.       
 35CL4c  Reaction products were detected using a Si detector telescope          
 35CL5c  consisting of a 250-|mm |DE-strip detector and a 1.5 -mm               
 35CL6c  surface-barrier E detector with FWHM=130 keV. Measured angular         
 35CL7c  distributions of cross sections |sE({+3}He),|q) and angular            
 35CL8c  distributions of analyzing powers iT{-11}(E({+3}He),|q). Deduced       
 35CL9c  levels, J, |p, L-transfers, and spectroscopic factors from DWBA        
 35CLAc  analysis of |s(E({+3}He),|q) and iT{-11}(E({+3}He),|q).                
